    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16288" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēthĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
		(scanned ĕthĭcīs,
			<i><span class="en">Prud. Hamart. 583</span></i>), adj., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠθικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>moral</i>, <i>ethic</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				<i>ethics</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					1, 2, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dictio,</span>”
				<i>which shows the character</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 11</span></i>
			.— Hence adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēthĭcos</span></b>  = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠθικῶς</span>, <i>morally</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dicere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 2, 12, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
